    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "34e5aa3b-db10-40a1-893d-79e98cd3f2f4",
      "key": "a0d70c65-6702-4def-a7fb-af8e70b2a9f1",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Features"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E4* hotel\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHalf board accommodation\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll excursions \u0026amp; guided tours included\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlue Badge guide Days 3 \u0026amp; 4\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExecutive coach throughout\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOne free place per 10 paying passengers\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "1d09b5af-b95a-4af5-b8f2-323db029e817",
      "key": "b9fb8ccb-074c-45ef-acf5-5265e0c01d5f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accommodation"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFour nights on half board basis at the 4* Park Royal Hotel at Stretton. Facilities at the hotel include a restaurant, bar and swimming pool. All rooms are en suite.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2d9b0603-29ef-423a-8d3e-d9c039d3d7b1",
      "key": "9c32e9b2-201d-41ec-874b-a44bc5a5ac7d",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECrich Tramway Village\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERHS Garden Bridgewater\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Silk Museum and Paradise Mill\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EQuarry Bank Mill and Styal Estate\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Anderton Boat Lift Visitor Centre\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Lowry\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlack Country Living Museum\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "de535189-b468-4594-8118-f303bac50e3c",
      "key": "3ee7b246-1774-4983-a857-39c33bc3fcb4",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tailor your sights"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EManchester Art Gallery\u003C/strong\u003E - home to one of the country\u2019s finest art collections including outstanding pre-Raphaelite paintings, craft and design, and early 20th century British art\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPontcysyllte Aqueduct\u003C/strong\u003E - a canal boat excursion across the famous Pontcysyllte Aqueduct built by Thomas Telford between 1795 and 1805\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ELyme Park property\u003C/strong\u003E - originally a Tudor house, Lyme was transformed by the Venetian architect Leoni into an Italianate palace, lavishly decorated with Mortlake tapestries and Grinling Gibbons wood carvings\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EThe Science \u0026amp; Industry Museum, Manchester\u003C/strong\u003E - traces the development of science, technology and industry with an emphasis on Manchester\u2019s achievements in these fields\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Here are some more suggested places of interest you might like to include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "2013b1b4-7597-48bb-963d-c31efa0924c8",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1 \u2013 Crich Tramway Village\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EBoard our private executive coach at your preferred pick up points \u2013 nestling high up in the heart of Derbyshire overlooking the famous Derwent Valley, Crich Tramway Village is a lovingly restored period village that is also home to the National Tramway Museum and its world renowned archives \u2013 check in at the 4* Park Royal Hotel at Stretton.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2 \u2013 RHS Garden Bridgewater\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA full day at RHS Garden Bridgewater, so named after the nearby canal \u2013 the Garden is the fifth RHS garden and at 156 acres is one of the largest gardening projects undertaken in Europe in recent years and brings back to life the lost historic grounds at Worsley New Hall in Salford \u2013 explore the kitchen, paradise and Chinese gardens, restored Victorian greenhouses and much more.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3 \u2013 The Silk Museum and Paradise Mill \u0026amp; Quarry Bank Mill and Styal Estate\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe Silk Museum and Paradise Mill reveals Macclesfield\u2019s 300 year story as a global centre for silk production, textiles and design and a guided tour of the Paradise Mill offers a unique insight into mill life and silk production \u2013 the restored Georgian cotton mill at Quarry Bank Mill and Styal Estate near Wilmslow tells the story of \u2018King Cotton\u2019 from a bale of raw cotton to finished cloth, and the original Apprentice House recreates the 1830s atmosphere of the lives of child workers.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4 \u2013 The Anderton Boat Lift Visitor Centre \u0026amp; The Lowry\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EA memorable boat trip along the River Weaver and through the Anderton Boat Lift, built by Edwin Clark in 1875 to lift cargo boats the 50 feet from the River Weaver to the Trent \u0026amp; Mersey Canal \u2013 set in a magnificent waterside location at the heart of the redeveloped Salford Quays, The Lowry houses the biggest public collection of works by LS Lowry with around 350 paintings and drawings, ranging across Lowry\u0026#39;s artistic career.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5 - Black Country Living Museum\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe award winning Black Country Living Museum, with period shops and houses set in a landscape of 26 acres, offers a glimpse into 300 years of history and reveals what it was like to live and work in one of the world\u2019s most industrialised landscapes.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Suggested Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Every one of our tours is exclusively for your group and your group alone so each one can be tailor made to suit the interests and profile of your members until you have a tour with an itinerary and at a price which matches the interests and profile of your members."
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "Remember this itinerary is just our suggestion. "
          }
        }
      ]
    },
